INTRODUCTION

This project was assigned as part of the Digital Literacy course to help students understand the importance of navigating the digital world responsibly and effectively. As a Student Digital Ambassador, the objective was to create a digital literacy portfolio that demonstrates awareness of online tools, platforms, communication methods, and cyber safety practices.
The project involved completing five tasks, including creating an infographic, building a digital portfolio, exploring coding and collaboration tools, practicing professional email etiquette, and studying cybercrime awareness. Through these activities, I gained practical knowledge of various digital platforms and developed essential skills required for academic and professional growth in the modern digital environment. 
TASK 1 : INFOGRAPHIC

For this task, I created a digital literacy awareness infographic using Canva. The infographic highlights key concepts such as the meaning of digital literacy, useful digital tools for students, safe internet practices, and the importance of maintaining a professional online presence.
I selected a clean and simple design template to ensure that the information is easy to read and visually appealing. The use of icons and short bullet points helped in presenting the content clearly and effectively.
One challenge I faced was selecting the most relevant information while keeping the design uncluttered. However, this task helped me understand how to communicate important ideas visually in a concise manner. It also improved my design and presentation skills.

 
TASK 2 : DIGITAL PORTFOLIO

In this task, I created profiles on GitHub and LinkedIn to establish my digital presence. GitHub is a platform used for hosting and sharing coding projects, while LinkedIn is a professional networking platform that helps connect with peers, mentors, and potential employers.
On GitHub, I created a profile README that includes my basic academic details and interests. On LinkedIn, I added my educational information, including my degree, institution, and expected graduation year.
I plan to use GitHub to upload my projects and track my learning progress in programming. LinkedIn will help me build a professional network, explore internship opportunities, and stay updated with industry trends over the next four years.
This task helped me understand the importance of building and maintaining a professional online identity from an early stage.

