TASK 4 : EMAIL ETIQUETTE
In this task, I practiced writing professional emails and created a social media etiquette checklist. Poor digital communication can lead to misunderstandings and may create a negative impression.
For example, sending an email without a proper subject line, greeting, or structure may appear unprofessional and could be ignored by the recipient. By following proper email etiquette, such as using a clear subject, respectful tone, and proper formatting, communication becomes more effective.
This task helped me understand the importance of professionalism in digital communication and how small details can make a big difference in conveying messages clearly.
 
TASK 5 : CYBERCRIME AWARENESS
While researching cybercrime, I was surprised by how common UPI fraud has become, especially with the increasing use of digital payments in India. Many people fall victim due to lack of awareness and trust in unknown sources.
I learned that scammers often trick users into approving payment requests or sharing sensitive information such as OTPs and PINs. These small mistakes can lead to serious financial loss.
As a result, I will be more cautious while making online transactions and will always verify requests before taking action. This task helped me understand the importance of staying alert and informed to ensure safety in the digital world.
 
CONCLUSION :

This project provided valuable insights into digital literacy and its importance in today’s world. Through various tasks, I learned about digital tools, professional communication, online collaboration, and cyber safety practices.
The project helped me develop practical skills that will be useful in both academic and professional environments. It also emphasized the importance of maintaining a responsible and secure online presence.
Overall, this assignment was a great learning experience that improved my understanding of the digital world and how to navigate it effectively.

